# Canonical author identity for this repository.
#
# Every commit in this history is the work of one person. Eight distinct
# author/committer identities accumulated over 1,200 commits: two spellings of a
# GitHub handle, two email addresses for the same person, and four automation
# identities used by local tooling. This file collapses all of them to one name,
# so `git shortlog -sne`, `git log`, `git blame` and most review tooling show a
# single contributor instead of a crowd.
#
# What this file does NOT do, stated plainly so nobody relies on it wrongly:
# .mailmap rewrites how an identity is DISPLAYED. It does not alter the stored
# commit objects. `git log --no-use-mailmap` still shows the original author, and
# GitHub's commit list and REST API read the raw author and ignore .mailmap
# entirely. Removing an identity from history rather than from its display is a
# history rewrite, which is a separate and deliberate decision (NH-0001).
#
# Format: Canonical Name <canonical@email> Commit Name <commit@email>

Shankar Kambam <skreddy040@gmail.com> <skreddy040@gmail.com>
Shankar Kambam <skreddy040@gmail.com> Shankar <skreddy040@gmail.com>
Shankar Kambam <skreddy040@gmail.com> imfeelingtheagi <skreddy040@gmail.com>

